    bottomLine: "The nearest Amazon match to the Perform Tread: a self-powered curved deck with eight magnetic levels, without the race-machine name or the sled handlebar.",
    description: "The Perform Tread is sold by Centr and dealers, not on Amazon. The C80 is the closest like-for-like machine we found there: a self-powered curved deck with a magnetic brake. The figures cross-checked on this site in October 2026 give it a 62 by 19-inch slat belt, eight magnetic resistance levels, a 330 lb maximum user weight and a 261 lb machine weight, and its Bluetooth console connects to SOLE’s own app and third-party platforms. Against the Perform Tread, it matches the belt width and the number of resistance levels, but it has no handlebar that converts to a sled-push station and a lower user rating. Its warranty is lifetime on the frame and one year on the deck, parts, electronics and labour, much shorter on parts than the Perform Tread’s seven years for home use. SOLE listed it at $2,399.99 on 5 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "sole-f63",
    name: "SOLE F63",
    brand: "SOLE",
    category: "Amazon Alternative to the Centr Runr",
    badge: "Amazon Alternative",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HFSXYZY4?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31Ka8IzhlWL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":333},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$1,100–$1,200",
    priceBounds: {"low":1100,"high":1200},
    specs: "20 x 60 in. deck · 0.5–12 mph · 0–15% incline · 325 lb capacity · folds",
    pros: [
      "A 60-inch deck, 12 mph and 325 lb, all above the Runr’s 55 inches, 10 mph and 300 lb",
      "Lifetime frame and motor warranty, as on the Runr, with two years on parts",
      "No monthly subscription; SOLE’s app is free",
      "SOLE and an independent review agree on deck, speed, incline, capacity and warranty",
    ],
    cons: [
      "No touchscreen, like the Runr",
      "The independent review notes it is a heavy machine",
      "Labour and deck terms are worth confirming with SOLE for the current model year",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For a folding treadmill on Amazon at the Runr’s price, with a longer deck and the same lifetime frame and motor cover.",
    description: "The Runr is sold by Centr and Costco rather than on Amazon. The SOLE F63 is the folding treadmill without a touchscreen we would compare it with there. SOLE lists a 20 by 60-inch running surface, 0.5 to 12 mph, 0 to 15% incline, a 325 lb maximum user weight and a 3.0 HP motor, and an independent review agrees on all of them. The warranty is lifetime on frame and motor and two years on parts, as SOLE’s own comparison table and the independent review both state; the review adds two years on the deck and wear items and one year of labour. That matches the Runr’s headline lifetime frame and motor cover, and the deck, speed and capacity figures are each a step above the Runr’s. It folds, and there is no subscription: SOLE’s app is free and the console works on its own. SOLE had it at $1,099.99 against a $1,199.99 regular price on 15 October, with a 30-day satisfaction guarantee and curbside delivery.",
  },
  {
    id: "nordictrack-t-series-16",
    name: "NordicTrack T Series 16",
    brand: "NordicTrack",
    category: "Amazon Alternative to the Centr Runr-S",
    badge: "Amazon Alternative With a Screen",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FBYJPXQ9?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31IJMmHM8RL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":491},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "Around $1,300–$2,000",
    priceBounds: {"low":1300,"high":2000},
    specs: "20 x 60 in. deck · 16 in. tilting touchscreen · 0-12% incline · up to 12 mph · 325 lb capacity",
    pros: [
      "A 16-inch touchscreen, larger than the Runr-S’s 10-inch screen",
      "A 60-inch deck and 12 mph, both above the Runr-S’s 55 inches and 10 mph",
      "SelectFlex cushioning and a low step-up",
      "Folds for storage",
    ],
    cons: [
      "The screen is built around iFIT classes rather than the Runr-S’s Netflix, YouTube and Disney+ apps",
      "No decline, a 20-inch belt and a 325 lb maximum user weight",
