  },
  {
    id: "sb-fitness-ct400",
    name: "SB Fitness CT400 Curved Treadmill",
    brand: "SB",
    category: "Lower-Priced Curved Trainer on Amazon",
    badge: "Curved Alternative",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08NK8YZJT?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31VKYCBmEYL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":375},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $1,595 (Amazon, 6 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":1595,"high":1595},
    specs: "Self-generated curved belt · 3 resistance levels · flexible track slats · no maximum speed",
    pros: [
      "The lowest price of the curved trainers on this page, at about $1,600",
      "No maximum speed and immediate response to speed changes, per the listing",
      "Three resistance levels for harder efforts",
      "Flexible track slats that the maker says add shock absorption",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Only three resistance levels, against eight on the Perform Tread and the SOLE C80",
      "The Amazon listing does not give deck dimensions or user capacity",
      "No sled-push mode, and a basic digital display",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The cheapest way on Amazon to try curved-treadmill running for HYROX-style intervals, if you can live with fewer resistance settings.",
    description: "For pure curved-treadmill running at a fraction of the Perform Tread’s price, the CT400 is the least expensive SB Fitness Equipment model we found on Amazon US. Its listing describes a self-generated curved treadmill designed for running, walking, sport-specific training and HIIT, with no maximum speed, three resistance levels, flexible track slats that SB Fitness says add shock absorption, quick response to speed changes and a front display showing time, distance, speed, calories and total miles. That covers the essentials for HYROX-style run intervals: a curved belt you drive yourself, so acceleration is limited only by you, and some resistance for harder pushes. What you give up is resistance range, with three levels rather than eight, and published detail: the Amazon listing does not give the running-surface size, the user capacity or the machine’s weight, so ask the seller for those before ordering, and measure your space. Amazon showed it at about $1,595 on 6 November 2026.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Brands", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/brands/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Centr Treadmills", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/centr-treadmills/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Who makes Centr treadmills?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Centr, the fitness brand founded by Chris Hemsworth, makes them with Inspire Fitness, a Southern California equipment maker. HighPost Capital acquired both companies in 2022 and combined them, which is why Costco lists Centr equipment as \"Centr by Inspire Fitness\". Centr’s store also sells Inspire Series treadmills.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much is the Centr x HYROX Perform Tread?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Centr and Perform Better both listed it at $6,999 on 5 November 2026. A Costco listing in search results showed $5,999, which we could not confirm on the day. Prices change, so check before buying.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What are the Centr x HYROX Perform Tread specs?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Centr and Perform Better agree on a motorless curved slat deck, a 59 by 19-inch running area, eight magnetic resistance levels, a 396.8 lb (180 kg) maximum user, a 400 lb assembled weight and a 74 by 42.5-inch footprint. Its height is listed as 67.3 inches by Centr and 59.2 inches by Perform Better.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the Centr Runr folding tool-less assembly treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It is Costco’s listing name for the Centr Runr, Centr’s folding motorized treadmill without a screen. Centr lists a 3.0 HP brushless motor, 1 to 10 mph, a 20 by 55-inch running surface, a 300 lb maximum user and tool-free setup, with a lifetime frame and motor warranty. Centr sold it for $1,299 on 5 November 2026.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the difference between the Centr Runr and Runr-S?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The Runr-S adds a 10-inch touchscreen with streaming apps, Bluetooth speakers, smartphone mirroring and 25 programs. The motor, deck, speed, 300 lb rating, footprint and warranty are the same. On 5 November 2026 Centr listed the Runr at $1,299 and the Runr-S at $1,699.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the Centr Runr good for running?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It suits walking and jogging better than running. Its 55-inch deck is short for taller runners at speed, the top speed is 10 mph and the rating is 300 lb, all below many treadmills at its price. Its strength is a lifetime warranty on the frame and motor.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the HYROX treadmill worth it for home use?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For a serious HYROX competitor who wants the race machine, it can be. For general curved-treadmill running, the TrueForm Trainer or AssaultRunner Pro cost about half as much, the SOLE C80, sold on Amazon, has eight magnetic resistance levels for about a third of the price, and the Tru Grit Runner offers sled-push settings for about a third of the price.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-05",
      dateModified: "2026-11-05",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 5,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/centr-treadmills/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/centr-treadmills/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "brands");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-05",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-05",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "centr treadmill",
      "centr runr treadmill",
      "centr runr folding tool-less assembly treadmill",
      "centr x hyrox perform tread motorless curved treadmill",
      "centr runr-s",
      "hyrox treadmill",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Closest on Amazon: SOLE C80 Curved Manual Treadmill", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/brands/">Brands</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Brand Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Centr Treadmills: Runr, Runr-S and the HYROX Perform Tread</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        Centr began as Chris Hemsworth’s fitness app and now sells home equipment made with Inspire Fitness, including the official HYROX race treadmill. Its treadmill range is short: two folding motorized Runr models and one motorless curved Perform Tread. Here is what each costs, the figures Centr and independent sources agree on, where they disagree, and who should buy which.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 5, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We research every product on this page independently. If you buy through our links, we may earn a
        commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Learn more about how we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#sole-c80"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31bmqOOpE8L._SL500_.jpg" alt="SOLE C80 Curved Manual Treadmill" width="500" height="333" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#sole-f63"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31Ka8IzhlWL._SL500_.jpg" alt="SOLE F63" width="500" height="333" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#nordictrack-t-series-16"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31IJMmHM8RL._SL500_.jpg" alt="NordicTrack T Series 16" width="500" height="491" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>SOLE C80 Curved Manual Treadmill · SOLE F63 · NordicTrack T Series 16</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          Centr is better known as an app than as an equipment brand: Chris Hemsworth launched it in 2019 as a
          workout and nutrition subscription. Since a 2022 deal that put Centr and Inspire Fitness, a Southern
          California equipment maker, under the same owner, it has sold home gyms, racks, weights and cardio
          machines under the Centr name, and since 2023 it has been the official equipment provider to HYROX,
          the indoor fitness race. On 5 November 2026 its US store listed three Centr treadmills — the Runr at
          $1,299, the Runr-S at $1,699 and the Official HYROX Perform Tread at $6,999 — plus Inspire Series
          treadmills sold alongside them. This guide covers each one and what to check before you buy.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest on Amazon:</span> <a href="#sole-c80">SOLE C80 Curved Manual Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Amazon Alternative:</span> <a href="#sole-f63">SOLE F63</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Amazon Alternative With a Screen:</span> <a href="#nordictrack-t-series-16">NordicTrack T Series 16</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Budget HYROX Alternative:</span> <a href="#tru-grit-runner">Tru Grit Runner Curved Manual Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Curved Alternative:</span> <a href="#sb-fitness-ct400">SB Fitness CT400 Curved Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[4].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
          <span class="ed-note-k">What we checked</span>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          5 November 2026 we read Centr's US store, including its full product catalogue and the product and
          specification pages for the Centr Runr, the Centr Runr-S and the Official HYROX Perform Tread (the
          Centr x HYROX Perform Tread). We cross-checked them against Perform Better's US listing for the
          Perform Tread, Costco's US listing for the Centr Runr Folding Tool-less Assembly Treadmill and
          Garage Gym Reviews' Runr-S and Perform Tread coverage (both seen only in search results; Costco
          refused our request and Garage Gym Reviews' pages would not load), other retailer listings in
          search results, trade-press reports of Centr's ownership and its HYROX partnership, and the US
          Consumer Product Safety Commission's recall database. Figures we give for Centr's machines are
          those on which Centr and at least one other source agree; conflicts are set out in the text. Centr's
          treadmills are not sold on Amazon, so the product cards show the closest Amazon alternatives, and
          their figures are the ones checked for our curved, budget and NordicTrack treadmill guides. Prices are Centr's own on the day unless stated, and change often. We have not tested any
          Centr treadmill and have no relationship with Centr or HYROX. As an Amazon Associate we earn from
          qualifying purchases; that does not change what we say.
        </aside>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="In this guide">
          <h2>In this guide</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#short-answer">Are Centr Treadmills Any Good? The Short Answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#who-is-centr">Who Makes Centr Treadmills?</a></li>
            <li><a href="#models">The Centr Treadmills, and Two Alternatives</a></li>
            <li><a href="#perform-tread">The Centr x HYROX Perform Tread in Detail</a></li>
            <li><a href="#runr">The Centr Runr and Runr-S in Detail</a></li>
            <li><a href="#inspire-series">The Inspire Series Treadmills on Centr’s Store</a></li>
            <li><a href="#where-to-buy">Where to Buy a Centr Treadmill</a></li>
            <li><a href="#which-to-buy">Which Centr Treadmill Should You Buy?</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Are Centr Treadmills Any Good? The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>The Centr x HYROX Perform Tread is a credible motorless curved treadmill and the one used
            at HYROX races, but at $6,999 it is worth it mainly for HYROX athletes. The Runr and Runr-S are
            ordinary folding treadmills — 3.0 HP, 10 mph, 300 lb — with a better-than-usual lifetime motor and
            frame warranty, best for walking and jogging.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            Centr's treadmill range, as listed on its US store on 5 November 2026, is three machines. The Runr
            ($1,299) and Runr-S ($1,699) are the same folding motorized treadmill with and without a 10-inch
            streaming touchscreen. The Official HYROX Perform Tread ($6,999) is a completely different kind of
            machine: a self-powered <a href="/curved-treadmill-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>curved treadmill</a> with magnetic resistance and a sled-push handlebar. Centr
            also sells four Inspire Series treadmills on the same store, which we cover briefly below.
          </p>
          <p>
            Two things are worth knowing up front. The Runr models are modest for their price on paper: a
            55-inch deck, 10 mph and a 300 lb rating are below what $1,300 to $1,700 buys from several other
            brands. And the Perform Tread, while it is the race machine, costs about twice as much as other
            well-regarded curved treadmills. We have not tested any Centr treadmill.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="who-is-centr" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Who Makes Centr Treadmills?</h2>
<p>
            Centr was founded by the actor Chris Hemsworth as a subscription app offering workouts, meal plans
            and mindfulness. In 2022 HighPost Capital, a private investment firm, acquired both Centr and Inspire
            Fitness, a home-equipment maker founded in Southern California in 2003, according to SGB Media and
            Athletech News, and the two businesses were combined. That is why Centr equipment is often listed as
            "Centr by Inspire Fitness", as Costco does, and why Centr's store sells Inspire Series treadmills and
            strength machines alongside Centr-branded ones.
          </p>
          <p>
            In October 2023 Centr became the official equipment provider of HYROX, the fitness race that
            alternates eight 1-kilometre runs with eight workout stations such as sled pushes, sled pulls and
            wall balls. Centr now supplies HYROX's sleds, wall balls, sandbags and <a href="/best-adjustable-kettlebells/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>kettlebells</a> and the Perform
            Tread, and sells the same equipment for home use. Every Centr purchase includes access to the Centr
            app; Centr's store listed the annual app subscription at $159.99 on its own.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Recalls</h3>
          <p>
            We searched the US Consumer Product Safety Commission's recall database for Centr, Inspire Fitness
            and HYROX on 5 November 2026 and found no recalls of Centr or Inspire treadmills. The search for
            "Centr" returns recalls from unrelated companies whose names contain those letters, such as
            Lenovo's ThinkCentre computers and Early Learning Centre toys; none is Centr's.
          </p>
        </div>

