              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Inspire Series T7s</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">As T7, with a 15.6 in. touchscreen</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$5,499</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            The T5 fixes the Runr's two main weaknesses, a 55-inch deck and a 10 mph ceiling, for $1,400 more;
            the T7 is a non-folding AC-motor machine aimed at serious runners. Centr lists lifetime frame and
            motor warranties on all four, with 7 years on parts for the T5 models and 10 for the T7 models. Our <a href="/best-treadmills-for-running/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best treadmills for running</a> and <a href="/best-treadmills-with-screens/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best treadmills with screens</a> cover what else that money buys.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="where-to-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Where to Buy a Centr Treadmill</h2>
<p>
            Centr sells direct through its own US store, and its treadmills also turn up at several retailers.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Centr.</strong> The Runr at $1,299, Runr-S at $1,699 and Perform Tread at $6,999 on
            5 November 2026. Each includes the Centr app.</li>
            <li><strong>Costco.</strong> Sells Centr equipment as "Centr by Inspire Fitness", including the
            Runr under the "Folding Tool-less Assembly" name and, at times, the Runr-S and Perform Tread. Costco
            prices can be well below Centr's — a $999.99 Runr-S deal was reported in December 2024 — but we
            could not see current Costco prices. Our <a href="/buying-a-treadmill-at-costco/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">guide to buying a treadmill at Costco</a> covers its delivery, returns and membership terms.</li>
            <li><strong>Academy Sports + Outdoors.</strong> Has listed the Runr and Runr-S and the Perform Tread;
            our <a href="/academy-sports-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Academy treadmills guide</a> has its range and policies.</li>
            <li><strong>Specialist dealers.</strong> Perform Better listed the Perform Tread at $6,999.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We did not find Centr treadmills sold new by Centr on Amazon US, which is why the cards on this
            page are Amazon alternatives rather than Centr models. If a Centr treadmill does turn up there from
            a third-party seller, check the seller and warranty before buying it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="which-to-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Which Centr Treadmill Should You Buy?</h2>
<ul>
            <li><strong>Walking and easy jogging, folds away:</strong> the Centr Runr at $1,299, for its lifetime
            frame and motor warranty and tool-free setup.</li>
            <li><strong>You want streaming on the treadmill:</strong> the Runr-S, but only if you will use the
            screen; otherwise put the $400 towards a longer deck.</li>
            <li><strong>You run regularly or are tall:</strong> skip the Runr models. The Inspire T5 on the same
            store has a 60-inch deck, or compare our running picks.</li>
            <li><strong>You are training for HYROX:</strong> the Perform Tread if budget allows; the Tru Grit
            Runner if it does not.</li>
            <li><strong>You want a curved treadmill for running and sprints:</strong> the TrueForm Trainer or <a href="/assaultrunner-pro-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">AssaultRunner Pro</a> at about
            half the Perform Tread's price, or, on Amazon, the SOLE C80 with eight magnetic levels or the cheaper
            SB Fitness CT400. Our <a href="/best-curved-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best curved treadmills</a> roundup compares them, and <a href="/curved-treadmill-workouts/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">curved treadmill workouts</a> has HYROX-style sessions.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Before you choose between a curved and a motorized machine at all, read our <a href="/manual-vs-motorized-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">manual vs. motorized treadmill guide</a>:
            a curved belt is hard work for long steady runs, and the Perform Tread will not replace a normal
            treadmill for easy miles.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Common mistakes -->
        <div id="common-mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Common Mistakes Buying a Centr Treadmill</h2>
          <p>Centr’s brand is strong and its treadmill range is narrow, which leads to a few predictable mismatches.</p>
          <ol class="ed-mistakes not-prose">
            <li>
              <h3>Buying the Runr for serious running</h3>
              <p>A 55-inch deck and a 10 mph top speed suit walking and jogging. Taller runners and anyone doing fast intervals should look at a treadmill with a 60-inch deck, including the Inspire T5 on Centr’s own store.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Paying for the screen you will not use</h3>
              <p>The Runr-S costs $400 more than the Runr for a 10-inch touchscreen. If you already watch a tablet or TV while you walk, the Runr does everything else the Runr-S does.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Buying the Perform Tread as an everyday treadmill</h3>
              <p>A motorless curved treadmill is hard work at any speed. It is superb for HYROX intervals and sled work, and tiring for long easy runs. If you want both, you may need a motorized treadmill as well, which changes the budget.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Measuring for the wrong height</h3>
              <p>Sellers list the Perform Tread’s height at 59.2, 65 or 67.3 inches. For a basement with a low ceiling or a tight doorway, plan for the tallest figure and ask the seller for shipping dimensions before ordering a 400 lb machine.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- The bottom line -->
        <div id="bottom-line" class="ed-bottomline">
          <h2>The bottom line</h2>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">Centr sells three treadmills: the folding Runr ($1,299) and Runr-S ($1,699),
          and the motorless Centr x HYROX Perform Tread ($6,999), the official HYROX race treadmill.</strong> The
          Runr models are walking and jogging treadmills with a better-than-usual lifetime frame and motor
          warranty but a short 55-inch deck and a 10 mph top speed.
          </p>
