          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the difference between the Centr Runr and Runr-S?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The Runr-S adds a 10-inch touchscreen with streaming apps, Bluetooth speakers, smartphone mirroring and 25 programs. The motor, deck, speed, 300 lb rating, footprint and warranty are the same. On 5 November 2026 Centr listed the Runr at $1,299 and the Runr-S at $1,699.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Centr Runr good for running?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It suits walking and jogging better than running. Its 55-inch deck is short for taller runners at speed, the top speed is 10 mph and the rating is 300 lb, all below many treadmills at its price. Its strength is a lifetime warranty on the frame and motor.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the HYROX treadmill worth it for home use?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For a serious HYROX competitor who wants the race machine, it can be. For general curved-treadmill running, the TrueForm Trainer or AssaultRunner Pro cost about half as much, the SOLE C80, sold on Amazon, has eight magnetic resistance levels for about a third of the price, and the Tru Grit Runner offers sled-push settings for about a third of the price.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

